WEBVTT

00:00:04.240 --> 00:00:11.240
<v Sarah Okafor>Morning, everyone. Monday the third of August. Can you all hear me, or am I doing the silent stand-up again?</v>

00:00:11.669 --> 00:00:20.070
<v Aisha Begum>Yeah, got you. I was just saying, my weekend plans were entirely dependent on that promised sunshine. Ended up watching rain from a caravan.</v>

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:26.320
<v Marcus Hale>That's a proper British holiday, that. Paid extra for the view of the rain?</v>

00:00:27.859 --> 00:00:33.810
<v Aisha Begum>Pretty much. Forecast for next weekend looks lovely, so obviously I don't believe a word of it.</v>

00:00:35.530 --> 00:00:41.829
<v Sarah Okafor>Quite. And apparently the charity bake sale on Friday is already causing arguments about what counts as homemade.</v>

00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:52.590
<v Marcus Hale>The charity bake sale on Friday is the only reason I've got cash in my wallet. Shop-bought cake on your own plate still counts, surely.</v>

00:00:53.109 --> 00:00:55.560
<v Callum Reid>Not with the price sticker underneath, mate.</v>

00:00:57.359 --> 00:01:02.960
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, before this becomes a cake audit. What's finished, and then what actually needs an owner?</v>

00:01:05.099 --> 00:01:12.099
<v Callum Reid>Yeah so, tested the water system yesterday and it's all fine now. That's finished, nothing new coming out of that.</v>

00:01:13.629 --> 00:01:16.430
<v Aisha Begum>Good. Nice to have one that's just closed.</v>

00:01:17.620 --> 00:01:23.569
<v Callum Reid>Also, already swapped the filter on the Injection Moulding Line 1 yesterday. That job's done as well.</v>

00:01:23.879 --> 00:01:33.329
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay. Separately, we still need someone to swap the filter on the line 1 hydraulics next Tuesday. It's urgent. Don't lose that against the completed filter entry.</v>

00:01:34.090 --> 00:01:40.739
<v Tomasz Nowak>Um, I'm not putting my hand up for that one. I haven't got the capacity to commit to it.</v>

00:01:41.640 --> 00:01:44.790
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Me neither, sorry. No offer from me on that.</v>

00:01:46.579 --> 00:01:51.480
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, nobody's taken it. The line 1 hydraulics filter stays unowned, urgent, next Tuesday.</v>

00:01:53.450 --> 00:02:03.250
<v Aisha Begum>And just for the history, I signed off the inspection on the feedwater pump on Tuesday. Last Tuesday, that was. Already signed off, not another inspection for today.</v>

00:02:03.930 --> 00:02:11.280
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks. Callum Reid, can you update the risk assessment for work on the Boiler Feedwater Pump? Separate from that completed inspection.</v>

00:02:11.919 --> 00:02:17.169
<v Callum Reid>Yeah, I'll update the risk assessment for work on the Boiler Feedwater Pump. That's mine.</v>

00:02:18.080 --> 00:02:21.930
<v Aisha Begum>Exactly, the inspection sign-off doesn't mean that risk assessment's been updated.</v>

00:02:22.949 --> 00:02:25.050
<v Sarah Okafor>Yep, two different things. That's clear.</v>

00:02:26.669 --> 00:02:36.469
<v Tomasz Nowak>While we're doing observations, noticed the IM3 was running a bit warm on nights but it settled down. Just an observation, I'm not raising a job off it.</v>

00:02:36.889 --> 00:02:40.740
<v Callum Reid>Right, settled down. Not another red box on the board, then.</v>

00:02:41.580 --> 00:02:49.979
<v Sarah Okafor>Still waiting on parts for the pick and place on two, nothing we can do until they arrive. That's the parts-dependent work still blocked.</v>

00:02:52.370 --> 00:02:57.620
<v Tomasz Nowak>Yeah. The guarding check is separate from doing the work that needs those parts, though.</v>

00:03:00.090 --> 00:03:07.090
<v Sarah Okafor>It is. Tomasz, can you check the guarding on the pick and place on two? Drop everything for that one.</v>

00:03:07.960 --> 00:03:13.210
<v Tomasz Nowak>Understood. I'll check the guarding on the pick and place on two. That takes precedence.</v>

00:03:14.819 --> 00:03:20.069
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Sorry, talking over you—so that's a check, not saying the blocked repair can go ahead?</v>

00:03:21.710 --> 00:03:26.960
<v Sarah Okafor>Correct. The parts blocker hasn't gone away. We're agreeing the guarding check, nothing beyond that.</v>

00:03:27.789 --> 00:03:35.139
<v Tomasz Nowak>And I'll schedule downtime for the GT2 with production by Wednesday. No rush on that one; it sits behind the guarding.</v>

00:03:36.710 --> 00:03:39.860
<v Callum Reid>Cheers, Tom. Scheduling with production by Wednesday, got it.</v>

00:03:41.919 --> 00:03:48.569
<v Tomasz Nowak>Yeah, just to be clear, by Wednesday is for scheduling it. I'm not saying the downtime itself is Wednesday.</v>

00:03:49.490 --> 00:03:56.490
<v Sarah Okafor>Hannah Price, can you take vibration readings on the gas turbine two on Friday, if you've got a spare minute?</v>

00:03:57.340 --> 00:04:03.639
<v Hannah Price>Yeah, I'll take vibration readings on the gas turbine two on Friday, if I've got a spare minute.</v>

00:04:04.719 --> 00:04:07.870
<v Marcus Hale>Right, that's the spare-minute one, not another drop-everything job?</v>

00:04:10.270 --> 00:04:13.770
<v Hannah Price>Exactly. On Friday, as agreed, but it's the spare-minute priority.</v>

00:04:14.750 --> 00:04:22.449
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Um, on the other hydraulic job, still waiting on parts for the IM1 hydraulic unit, nothing we can do until they arrive.</v>

00:04:22.819 --> 00:04:31.569
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay. I'll replace the seals on the IM1 hydraulic unit at half two. That's my agreed job, but it is still blocked by those parts.</v>

00:04:33.569 --> 00:04:40.220
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Right, Saz, at half two, but only possible if the parts have arrived. I'm not confirming a delivery there.</v>

00:04:40.759 --> 00:04:47.410
<v Sarah Okafor>Absolutely. Mine at half two, with that blocker showing. I'm not pretending we can replace seals we haven't got.</v>

00:04:48.339 --> 00:04:52.189
<v Callum Reid>Fine. An agreed time isn't a promise from the supplier. Understood.</v>

00:04:54.189 --> 00:05:05.389
<v Sarah Okafor>And we were going to replace the belt on the main water valve but that's been pushed to next month, so ignore it. Cancelled from this lot, not a job for today.</v>

00:05:07.579 --> 00:05:12.129
<v Marcus Hale>Yep. That old entry was making the list look longer than it is.</v>

00:05:14.540 --> 00:05:18.040
<v Hannah Price>I'll do the pre-use checks on the FLTs next Tuesday.</v>

00:05:19.360 --> 00:05:24.959
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, Han. That one's safety critical, straight away. For next Tuesday, those checks come before use.</v>

00:05:27.439 --> 00:05:33.740
<v Hannah Price>Agreed. Next Tuesday, I'll do the pre-use checks on the FLTs straight away, before they're used. Safety critical.</v>

00:05:34.079 --> 00:05:40.029
<v Callum Reid>So we're keeping next Tuesday, not accidentally dragging that date into today because we've said straight away?</v>

00:05:41.800 --> 00:05:46.699
<v Hannah Price>Yes, next Tuesday. Straight away for the pre-use checks then, not a different date.</v>

00:05:48.399 --> 00:05:55.050
<v Sarah Okafor>Han, can you also grease and check the bearings on the water booster tomorrow morning? Low priority, that one.</v>

00:05:57.480 --> 00:06:03.079
<v Hannah Price>Yeah, I'll grease and check the bearings on the water booster tomorrow morning. Low priority, understood.</v>

00:06:03.680 --> 00:06:08.230
<v Callum Reid>And that's separate maintenance from my water system test yesterday. Test's still done.</v>

00:06:08.750 --> 00:06:11.199
<v Sarah Okafor>Exactly. We're not reopening your completed test.</v>

00:06:11.699 --> 00:06:17.300
<v Sarah Okafor>I'll recalibrate the sensors on the air dryer by Thursday. That one's safety critical, straight away.</v>

00:06:19.639 --> 00:06:25.240
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Okay, Sarah Okafor against the air dryer sensor recalibration, by Thursday. That's you owning it, yeah?</v>

00:06:26.339 --> 00:06:31.939
<v Sarah Okafor>Yes, me. I'll start straight away because it's safety critical, with the recalibration done by Thursday.</v>

00:06:33.970 --> 00:06:42.720
<v Aisha Begum>There's quite a spread there. Safety critical, drop everything, and then genuinely low priority. Easy to hear them all as urgent on a crackly call.</v>

00:06:44.189 --> 00:06:47.689
<v Sarah Okafor>Yeah, don't flatten the priorities. They're different for a reason.</v>

00:06:49.149 --> 00:06:54.399
<v Marcus Hale>Speaking of crackly, is that someone's mic rubbing, or am I hearing a crisp packet?</v>

00:06:55.879 --> 00:06:59.029
<v Tomasz Nowak>Headset cable. Bit early even for my breakfast crisps.</v>

00:07:00.889 --> 00:07:10.689
<v Sarah Okafor>Before we finish: swap the filter on the line 1 hydraulics, next Tuesday, it's urgent. Still nobody on it; we haven't magically allocated it by talking about it.</v>

00:07:11.319 --> 00:07:18.670
<v Callum Reid>And don't put me down from the yesterday update. The Injection Moulding Line 1 filter swap I mentioned was completed work.</v>

00:07:21.019 --> 00:07:23.120
<v Sarah Okafor>Correct. The outstanding one remains unallocated.</v>

00:07:24.800 --> 00:07:34.600
<v Hannah Price>I've got my three clear: water booster tomorrow morning, gas turbine two on Friday if I've got a spare minute, and FLTs next Tuesday, safety critical before use.</v>

00:07:36.930 --> 00:07:42.180
<v Tomasz Nowak>Same here. Guarding first, drop everything. GT2 downtime scheduling by Wednesday, no rush on that.</v>

00:07:44.490 --> 00:07:49.740
<v Olumide Adeyemi>And the parts blockers are still blockers. Nothing said on this call means they've arrived.</v>

00:07:51.699 --> 00:07:53.800
<v Sarah Okafor>Agreed. Right, that's us. Thanks, everyone.</v>
